// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// A Table body is `milestoneSpec? (columnDefinition (COMMA columnDefinition)*)?`. The
// milestoning block must come FIRST, before any column. This declares the columns and then
// the milestoning that describes them.
//
// Reading order argues for exactly this file: you cannot say a column is the business-from
// date until the column exists. The grammar disagrees, and it disagrees silently -- a
// rewrite that treats a Table body as a list of entries and sorts out which is which
// afterwards accepts both orders. Moving the block above the columns makes this parse.
###Relational
Database fixture::neg::MilestoningLate
(
   Table T
   (
      ID VARCHAR(32) PRIMARY KEY,
      SNAP DATE,
      milestoning
